## Why This Is Asked

Targets hallucination risk, retrieval provenance, and privacy in a real-time multilingual setting, a practical pain point in enterprise support.

## Key Concepts

- Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) with private KB
- On-device inference, edge caching, latency budgeting
- Multi-language alignment and provenance tokens
- Hallucination detection, data redaction, drift monitoring

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: integrate on-device summarizer with retrieval module
async function summarize(chatChunk, kb) {
  const onDeviceSummary = await onDeviceModel.encodeDecode(chatChunk);
  const docs = kb.lookup(chatChunk, topK=5);
  const finalSummary = await ragGenerate(onDeviceSummary, docs);
  return { summary: finalSummary.text, provenance: finalSummary.provenance };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you quantify and mitigate factual drift in multilingual outputs?
- What rollback strategy and audit trail would you implement for regulatory compliance?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical, on-device NLP that yields actionable summaries from multilingual consumer reviews, a realistic Instacart/Amazon use case, without network dependency.

## Key Concepts
- On-device multilang NLP under tight size constraints
- Feature extraction via lightweight POS or rules
- Sentiment aggregation and justification
- Privacy-first data labeling and offline evaluation

## Code Example
```javascript
function scoreFeature(feature, sentences) {
  let score = 0;
  for (const s of sentences) {
    if (s.toLowerCase().includes(feature)) {
      if (/\b(good|great|excellent|loved)\b/.test(s)) score += 1;
      if (/\b(bad|worst|terrible|hate)\b/.test(s)) score -= 1;
    }
  }
  return score;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle negation and language switch within a single sentence?
- How would you validate usefulness of summaries to buyers?
